# Git commit author

When creating git commits for this project, the author must always be:

**Abinash** `<mrabinash2022@gmail.com>`

## How to commit

Do **not** change `git config`. Pass author explicitly on every commit:

```bash
git commit --author="Abinash <mrabinash2022@gmail.com>" -m "..."
```

On Windows PowerShell, use a here-string for multiline messages with `-F -` and still pass `--author`:

```powershell
git commit --author="Abinash <mrabinash2022@gmail.com>" -F -
```

Alternatively, set env vars for that command only:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Abinash" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="mrabinash2022@gmail.com" GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Abinash" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="mrabinash2022@gmail.com" git commit -m "..."
```

## Verify before push

After committing, confirm authorship:

```bash
git log -1 --format="%an <%ae>"
```

Expected: `Abinash <mrabinash2022@gmail.com>`
